# Thread-assisted-Port-scanner-777

Python Port Scanner

A simple and lightweight TCP Port Scanner written in Python. This tool allows users to scan specified ports on a target IP address or hostname and identify whether they are open or closed.

Features
TCP Port Scanning: Checks the connection status of specified TCP ports.
Custom Port Selection: Scan individual ports or multiple ports (e.g. 80,443,22).
Service Response Detection: Attempts to retrieve service response data from open ports.
Timeout Support: Uses a 1-second connection timeout.
Thread Support: Uses Python's ThreadPoolExecutor.
Colored Terminal Output: Provides a simple and readable terminal interface.
Error Handling: Handles invalid ports, hostnames, timeouts, and keyboard interruptions.
Requirements
Python 3.x
No external libraries required.
Installation

Clone the repository:

bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/python-port-scanner.git


Navigate to the project directory:

bash
cd python-port-scanner

Usage

Run the script:

bash
python portscanner.py


Enter the target IP address or hostname:

text
[?] Please enter target IP : 127.0.0.1


Enter the ports you want to scan:

text
[?] Please enter your ports (EX: 80,443,22) : 80,443,22,8080

